---
title: Bagels
servings: 12
yield: 8 large or 12 standard bagels
tags: [jewish, vegan, weekend]
time: 2 hours 50 minutes
source: Bagels by PJ Hamel, King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/bagels-recipe
---

== Dough ==

Knead the @instant yeast{9%g}, @bread flour{480%g}, @table salt{12%g}, @non-diastatic malt powder{9%g}(or 14 g dark brown sugar) and @water{303%g}(lukewarm) ~{10%minutes} in a #stand mixer{}, or up to 15 minutes by hand. The dough is stiff.

Cover it in a lightly greased bowl and leave ~{1%hour} to 1 1/2 hours, until clearly puffy.

Grease two #baking sheets{} or line them with parchment. Divide the dough into 8 or 12 pieces and roll each into a smooth ball. Set them on one sheet, cover and rest ~{30%minutes}.

== Boil and bake ==

Heat the oven to 425°F (220°C). In a #wide pan{}, bring the @water{1814%g}, @non-diastatic malt powder{18%g}(or 28 g dark brown sugar) and @granulated sugar{14%g} to a very gentle boil.

Push a finger through the middle of each ball and stretch the hole to 1 1/2 to 2 inches. Put six on each sheet.

Boil four at a time ~{2%minutes}, flip them and boil ~{1%minute} more. Lift them out with a #skimmer{} back onto the sheet.

Bake ~{20%minutes} to 25 minutes, turning them over about 15 minutes in. Cool completely on a #wire rack{} before cutting.

> For seeded bagels, brush them before baking with an egg white beaten with
> 1 tbsp water and scatter thickly with sesame or poppy seeds.
